From 07f795dfed0d55cbb4d2d366d77102d5335046d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:06:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Calls between the person's computers take the Tailscale road
 first, each end proving it's theirs

Every connection between the person's computers needed the edge: the
relay goes through it, and the WebRTC link is set up through it, so the
first call to a device waited on Cloudflare (72-295 ms to connect from
home) and an edge outage stopped their computers working together though
Tailscale reached each in 4-90 ms.

- A listener on the Tailscale address only, re-bound as it changes, written
  to the device row (endpoints, direct-tcp-v1); on by default, off with
  ZERON_TAILNET=0 or tailnet-road.json's "enabled": false.
- A mutual signed challenge with Zeron device keys before any call; a
  verified caller is served as that device, under the relay's guard.
- Links served as a proven device's, on any road, are checked again (every
  60 s, on list or key changes) and closed once their device no longer
  stands, or after an hour.
- First among the roads; a dead address costs about a second; with the
  edge down, cached addresses and keys keep desktops working together.
- Cloud machines and the phone neither listen nor dial.

Tests: tailnet::handshake's 17, tailnet::address's 5, tailnet's 15,
direct_rpc::tailnet_road's 1, device_endpoints' 1, direct_rpc's 1,
tailnet_road's 8, edge_down's 5.
